---
import ContentGrid from "../structure/ContentGrid.astro";
import ContentSection from "../structure/ContentSection.astro";
---

<!-- The library's visitor-facing copy comes from trunk's homepage and support
     page. Keep #library stable: it is linked from both of those pages. -->
<ContentSection id="library" title="Seattle Library" headingLevel="h2">
  <ContentGrid columns={2}>
    <r-cell span="1">
      <p>
        The Connections Museum Seattle operates a reference library of
        information related to our region and the equipment we maintain.
        Contributions of materials greatly appreciated. Digitization of our
        technical documentation is available upon request.
      </p>
      <p>
        While we don't yet have a proper archival environment in Seattle,
        we still maintain an extensive collection of printed material related
        to the history of telephony, and especially technical material
        required for maintaining our equipment, which we try our best to make
        available to the broader telephone collector community.
      </p>
    </r-cell>
    <r-cell span="1">
      <p>
        If the documents are of a technical nature, relate to the history of
        the Pacific Northwest, Seattle, or most especially the Panel Switch
        (<i>anything marked "Full Mechanical"</i>) then please contact
        <a href="mailto:library@connections.museum">library@connections.museum</a>.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/support.html#equipment-donations">More about donating equipment or historical documents.</a></p>
    </r-cell>
  </ContentGrid>
</ContentSection>
